  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1330",
      "html": "<ul><li>Scientific name: Hypostomus pyrineusi (Miranda Ribeiro, 1920)</li><li>Type locality: Jamary, Rio Madeira, Amazon system, Brazil.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/loricariidae/hypostomus_pyrineusi.htm",
      "html": "<ul><li>Common name: Madeira pleco</li><li>IUCN Red List: Least Concern (IUCN 2023)</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1330",
      "html": "<p>South America: Madeira River basin (?). Amazon, Middle Amazon (Solimoes), Madeira.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/loricariidae/hypostomus_pyrineusi.htm",
      "html": "<p>South America: Madeira, Napo, Ucayali, Marañon and upper Amazon River basins. Type locality: probably Jamary [Brazil].</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/loricariidae/hypostomus_pyrineusi.htm",
      "html": "<p>As with most of this genus, it will do well in a larger aquarium of 120 cm or over, well filtered.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/loricariidae/hypostomus_pyrineusi.htm",
      "html": "<p>Water parameters can be quite diverse for this genus.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/loricariidae/hypostomus_pyrineusi.htm",
      "html": "<p>Omnivore with a liking for green, tablet and frozen foods. This species is also a lover of wood, which should be provided in the aquarium.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/loricariidae/hypostomus_pyrineusi.htm",
      "html": "<p>Peaceful species that will dig up plants with its constant burrowing in the substrate, so it is better to put plants in pots.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1330",
      "html": "<p>Breeding: Unreported.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1330",
      "html": "<p>Previously placed in Cochliodon and now included in the larger genus Hypostomus as a member of the Hypostomus Cochliodon group. All these species have higher backs than other conspecifics and spoon shaped teeth (like Panaque).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/loricariidae/hypostomus_pyrineusi.htm",
      "html": "<p>Placed in the Hypostomus cochliodon species group, which have a shorter, higher-backed body than other members of Hypostomus. They have a small number of spatulate teeth with a single cusp, with the jaws arranged in a V shape. Hypostomus have 7 dorsal fin rays, whereas the similar-looking Pterygoplichthys have 10. Hypostomus pyrineusi is distinguished from most members of the H. cochliodon group by having 0–10 (usually 0) odontodes on the opercle, large spoon-shaped teeth, no buccal papilla, no strong sharp keels on the lateral plates, an adipose fin, numerous close-set spots on the body, and pigmentation equally distributed on the lobes of the caudal fin (Armbruster 2003).</p><p>Etymology: the specific name pyrineusi honours Miranda Ribeiro's good friend Lieut. Antonio Pyrineus de Souza (d. 1936), a naturalist with the Rondon Commission, which installed telegraph poles from Mato Grosso to Amazonas, on an expedition that collected the type.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "references",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1330",
      "html": "<p>Peixes (excl. Characinidae) No. 58 (Annexo 5), pp 9, Unnum. Pls. 3-4.</p>"
    }
